Description Task 1: Import the assert.yml file to perform preconditions checks. This task should only run once and is delegated to localhost.

Task 2: Install mysql
Description Task 2: Install MySQL using the package module. This task will notify handlers to set the root password and re-exec the daemon.

Task 3: Configure mysql server
Description Task 3: Configure the MySQL server by modifying the server configuration file using the ini_file module. The task iterates over the options defined in the variable mysql_configuration_options and notifies a handler to restart the MySQL server if changes are made.

Task 4: Configure mysql client
Description Task 4: Configure the MySQL client by setting the socket option in the client configuration file using the ini_file module.

Task 5: Initialize mysql
Description Task 5: Initialize MySQL on specific distributions (Alpine and Archlinux) using a command that creates the MySQL data directory.

Task 6: Start and enable mysql
Description Task 6: Start and enable the MySQL service using the service module. This task ensures the MySQL service is running and set to start on boot.

Task 7: Flush handlers
Description Task 7: Flush any pending handlers to ensure they are executed immediately.

Task 8: Place my.cnf
Description Task 8: Place the my.cnf file in the root user's home directory using a template. The mode is set to 0640.

Task 9: Create databases
Description Task 9: Create MySQL databases based on the list provided in the variable mysql_databases. The task uses a loop, and conditions are set to ensure that databases are only created if initial_import is not defined.

Task 10: List databases
Description Task 10: List existing databases using the mysql_info module. The result is registered in the mysql_info variable.

Task 11: Import database
Description Task 11: Import databases that are flagged for initial import in the mysql_databases variable. The task ensures the database does not already exist before importing.

Task 12: Create users
Description Task 12: Create MySQL users based on the list provided in the variable mysql_users. The task uses a loop and ensures user creation only if the mysql_users variable is defined.

Task 13: Flush handlers again
Description Task 13: Flush any pending handlers again to ensure all are executed.


